@startuml seq-reload-safe-refresh
'' PlantUML over Mermaid: the point is the ORDER of events across a writer, main's single-flight read and two
'' windows — a burst of writes during one read, a torn PDF settled with backoff, one read fanned out, and a late
'' read dropped by its number. A sequence diagram with alt branches states exactly that. Brown = the file being
'' written, slate = main (the watcher, the content-flight model, the verified reader), teal = the windows.
!include _vv-theme.iuml

title ADR-0046 — a deck rewritten while two windows show it: one read, verified, numbered, fanned out

participant "writer\n(pdflatex)" as W FS_TINT
participant "change source\n(chokidar · ADR-0035 daemon)" as N MAIN_TINT
participant "content-flight\n(pure model)" as F MAIN_TINT
participant "verified reader\n(readPdf* · settlePdf)" as R MAIN_TINT
participant "window A" as A RENDERER_TINT
participant "window B" as B RENDERER_TINT

== a burst of writes: one read, one trailing read ==
W -> N : write (compile starts)
N -> F : change
F -> R : [:read path seq=7]
activate R
W -> N : write, write, write (during the read)
N -> F : change × 3 → the read is marked DIRTY\n(exactly one trailing read, however many)

== the verified read ==
R -> R : tail first: no final %%EOF → torn
loop backoff u, 2u, 4u, 8u (woken early by a change)
  R -> R : tail → body → fstat on the same handle:\nsize + mtime unchanged? verdict complete?
end
alt complete
  R --> F : bytes
  F -> A : vv:content {seq 7}
  F -> B : vv:content {seq 7}
  note right of B #E3F2ED: one read delivered to every\nretaining window (1.003 S per change)
else still changing, and a notification will announce the next write
  R --> F : pending — the requesters wait for the next read
else stable but incomplete (a LaTeX error), or changing with no notification coming
  R --> F : incomplete {reason}
  F -> A : vv:content {seq 7, incomplete}
  note right of A #F5E1E0: A shows a complete version:\nit KEEPS it, behind a note
end
deactivate R

== the trailing read, and a late arrival ==
F -> R : [:read path seq=8] (the dirty mark)
activate R
R --> F : bytes (complete)
deactivate R
F -> A : vv:content {seq 8}
F -> B : vv:content {seq 8}
A -> A : content-guard: 8 > applied 7 → apply;\npdf replace-doc! in place, the slide kept
note over A, B #E3F2ED: a read that lands late with seq ≤ the applied one is DROPPED —\nthe display never moves backwards

legend right
  |= Colour |= Concept |
  |<#9F8766>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the file being written |
  |<#3A5BA0>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| main: change source, content-flight, verified reader |
  |<#2D9574>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| renderer windows |
  u = 250 ms; seq is minted only by main.
endlegend
@enduml
